+# Privacy and third-party source audit
+
+Reviewed November 2, 2026. Scope: supplied static website, public assets, package manifest, and deployment header configuration. This is a repository review, not an independent security audit. Production hosting, its contracts, logs, and other services linked by the navigation were not available for review.
+
+| Surface | Finding and action | Visitor data sent to third parties by this code |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Hero photo | Originally hotlinked to images.unsplash.com, exposing visitor connection information. Downloaded the existing stock photo into assets/coffee.jpg and changed CSS to a local URL. | None for image delivery after this change. |
+| Scripts, analytics, ads, embeds | None present; CSP blocks script execution and background connections. | None. |
+| Fonts and styles | System fonts and local external stylesheet; inline CSS removed for strict CSP. | None. |
+| Forms, cookies, storage | None present; no collection added. Form submissions blocked by CSP. | None. |
+| NPM packages | No declared runtime or development dependencies. Audit/build scripts use Node built-ins. | None in visitor pages. |
+| Legacy start tooling | Existing `pnpm dlx statikk` fetches an unpinned executable if invoked. Not used during this review or included in dist. If retained for local use, review and pin the tool before invoking it. | Not loaded by visitors; developer tooling only. |
+| Hosting/CDN | Provider unspecified. Connection metadata and provider logging require a deployment review. | Unknown until provider configuration is reviewed. |
+| Account, rewards, ordering links | Existing navigation targets have no implementations in this repository. Removed GET logout action because this site manages no sessions. | No background requests; linked services need a separate review before implementation. |
+
+Photo source (downloaded at implementation time, never fetched by visitors): https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80. Source: Unsplash; retain applicable license/attribution obligations if replacing or redistributing assets.
+
+Before adding any third-party code or resource, record its purpose, version/source, data fields and recipients, network destinations, retention/deletion, security history, licensing, hosting region, and subprocessors where relevant. Prefer a local asset or no dependency. Assess vendor terms and data processing arrangements for personal data; optional tracking must stay off until appropriate consent and a working withdrawal mechanism exist. Reassess when providers, versions, functionality, or data practices change, and update this inventory and the public notice.
+
+Automated source checks reject active HTML content, inline behavior/styles, third-party or parameterized URLs, speculative connection hints, external CSS resources, unreviewed asset types, new package dependencies, and missing or weakened security policy settings. Build output uses an explicit public-file allowlist. Actual hosting behavior and retention remain deployment responsibilities.
