+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static HTML and CSS, with a locally hosted photograph. No runtime JavaScript, forms, accounts, analytics, browser storage, or package dependencies are needed to render these pages.
+
+Run `npm run audit:privacy` for the source privacy audit or `npm run build` to audit and create `dist/`. Both use only Node built-ins and start no servers. Publish only `dist/`, not the repository root. The build excludes source tooling and documentation.
+
+## Security headers and deployment
+
+`_headers` supplies response headers for static hosts that support this format, including Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. Deploy `dist/` over HTTPS and enforce an HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect at the host. On other hosts, configure the equivalent response headers in the hosting platform before release. The legacy `start` script uses a network-downloaded static server; it is not the production deployment path and is not expected to apply `_headers`.
+
+The response CSP blocks scripts, API/background connections, frames, workers, plugins, and submissions; it permits only local images and styles. Header-only framing protection is provided by `frame-ancestors` and `X-Frame-Options`. HTML includes CSP and referrer fallbacks for hosts that omit headers, but these **do not replace response headers**. Permissions Policy denies sensitive browser features, referrer policy suppresses referring URLs, and `nosniff` prevents MIME sniffing. HSTS covers the deployed hostname without committing other subdomains. `no-store` avoids caching page responses; this does not delete hosting logs or existing browser data.
+
+Before production release, the deployment owner must confirm that HTTPS, redirects, MIME types, and the headers are actually applied to successful and error responses. Source checks cannot verify a hosting provider. No browser verification, HTTP server, or preview server was used for this change.
+
+## Data handling
+
+Keep the site script-free unless a reviewed feature needs data. Do not put personal data, session identifiers, or secrets in HTML, URLs, browser storage, console output, analytics, or CSP reports. There is no data collection endpoint and no optional tracking that needs a consent banner. Do not add a banner that implies tracking exists.
+
+The old GET logout link was removed: this static site has no session to terminate. If accounts or ordering are implemented, review them separately: state changes (including logout) need POST with CSRF protection; sessions belong in Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookies; validate input on the server, minimize collected fields, restrict access, and define deletion and retention before collection. Never handle payment credentials in this static site.
+
+Hosting providers necessarily process connection data. Configure minimal access logs, redact query strings and credentials, limit operator access, and document a short justified retention period with the provider. The repository cannot enforce these provider settings. Update the public privacy notice with actual provider, contact, and retention details when deployment information is available. Do not promise zero logging or claim regulatory compliance based on this code.
+
+## Third-party review
+
+See [PRIVACY-AUDIT.md](PRIVACY-AUDIT.md) for the current inventory, findings, and review criteria. Re-run the audit on every change. It is a conservative static guardrail, not a full HTML parser, vulnerability scanner, independent certification, or infrastructure assessment.
+
+References: [Cloudflare header configuration](https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/), [CSP header](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy), [header-only frame-ancestors](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/frame-ancestors), [referrer policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Referrer-Policy).
